<title>SINGAPORE: India offers Mar 1-3 Cochin high aromatic naphtha.</title>
<headline>India offers Mar 1-3 Cochin high aromatic naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has offered in a tender 30,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha (HAN) lifting March 1-3 from Cochin on the east coast, industry sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes February 20 and is valid until the February 21.</p>
<p>IOC's last HAN tender from Cochin, lifting January 29-31, was awarded at $20.98 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
